     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the maximum labeled dose of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. The single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg per dose. At this level the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg total daily**, split into smaller doses (for example 850 mg twice daily)\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
